素类, including 利福布汀 and 利福平, significantly reduce plasma concentrations of protease inhibitors (PIs) and NNRTIs by inducing CYP3A4 metabolism [Data: Relationships (30267, 30508)]. For example, 利福平 is contraindicated with all PIs due to profound reductions in drug exposure, while 利福布汀 may be used with dose adjustments (e.g., 150 mg three times weekly with LPV/r) [Data: Relationships (30267)]. These interactions pose a high risk of virologic failure and development of drug resistance in HIV patients if not properly managed [Data: Relationships (30508)]. Guidelines recommend selecting antiretrovirals with minimal interaction profiles—such as efavirenz—or substituting 利福平 with 利福布汀 in co-infected individuals.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"利福布汀 is associated with specific adverse reactions requiring clinical monitoring\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Clinical use of 利福布汀 is linked to notable adverse effects, including 中心粒细胞减少症 (neutropenia) and 葡萄膜炎 (uveitis) [Data: Entities (15288, 16613, 17278); Relationships (9314, 9316, 9319)]. Evidence indicates that when 利福布汀 is co-administered with boosted PIs like LPV/r, its exposure increases, heightening the risk of these toxicities [Data: Relationships (9314, 9319)]. Therefore, guidelines emphasize regular monitoring of complete blood counts and ophthalmologic evaluations during combination therapy, particularly in HIV/TB co-infected pediatric and adult patients [Data: Relationships (9314)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"抗HIV药物 and 抗结核药物 exhibit broad and clinically critical interactions\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The interaction between 抗HIV药物 and 抗结核药物 represents a major challenge in managing HIV/TB co-infection [Data: Entities (10881, 10989); Relationships (38453)]. Rifamycins—core anti-TB agents—induce metabolic enzymes that lower concentrations of key antiretrovirals, risking subtherapeutic levels [Data: Relationships (30508, 38453)]. Conversely, some antiretrovirals (e.g., efavirenz) can also alter TB drug levels (e.g., reducing bedaquiline concentrations) [Data: Relationships (30508)]. Structured guidance, including dose modifications and therapeutic drug monitoring, is essential to mitigate these risks and ensure dual treatment success [Data: Relationships (38453)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Use of rifamycins is contraindicated or requires caution in transplant recipients\",\n            \"explanation\": \"抗结核药物, particularly rifamycins, are contraindicated or require extreme caution in 实体器官移植受者 (solid organ transplant recipients) due to interactions with immunosuppressants like tacrolimus (FK506) [Data: Entities (14590); Relationships (6403, 28270)]. Although one study suggested NNRTIs have minimal effect on FK506 levels, rifamycins can significantly alter the pharmacokinetics of calcineurin inhibitors, potentially leading to graft rejection or toxicity [Data: Relationships (6403)]. Thus, alternative TB regimens avoiding strong CYP inducers are often recommended in this vulnerable population [Data: Relationships (6403)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Rifamycins interact with non-antiretroviral medications, including hypoglycemics and cardiovascular drugs\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Beyond antiretrovirals, 利福霉素 interact with diverse drug classes, including sulfonylurea hypoglycemics like 瑞格列齐 and cardiovascular agents [Data: Entities (6889); Relationships (30501)]. Evidence shows rifamycins induce glucuronidation and CYP-mediated metabolism, reducing exposure to drugs such as 瑞格列齐, necessitating dose increases and close glucose monitoring [Data: Relationships (30501)]. Similarly, interactions with warfarin, calcium channel blockers, and ACE inhibitors may require therapeutic adjustments to maintain efficacy and safety [Data: Relationships (30501)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Other antiretrovirals like 地拉夫定 affect methadone pharmacokinetics\",\